patches/ -- source overlays applied at build time
=================================================

One subdirectory per component, one .patch per change. The patches never touch
src/: the build applies them with `patch -p1` to a throwaway copy of the
source. The prose above each diff says what the change is and why it is
carried here rather than upstream.

The directory says which toolchain applies a patch:

    patches/<component>/        both toolchains (the hv/ patches name their
                                path below); changes the product
    patches/<component>/gnu/    gnu path only; changes nothing in the product
                                (verified byte for byte, tests/full/obp/TESTS)
                                and exists so Sun's sources build on a
                                GNU/Linux host at all
    patches/<component>/sun/    sun path only

The components:

    patches/obp/forth/    Forth/FCode source, applied by build/obp.mk (sun
                          path) and build/obp/gnu/obp-gnu.mk (gnu path) to a
                          copy of src/obp
    patches/obp/gnu/      C source of the Forth engine and the OBMD host
                          tools, applied by build/obp/gnu/engine/Makefile
    patches/obp/sun/      the sun path's build tree, applied by build/obp.mk
    patches/hv/           applied by build/hv_reset.mk (and, on the gnu path,
                          build/hv_reset/gnu/build.sh) to a copy of
                          src/hypervisor
    patches/hv/gnu/       the gnu path's own, applied by
                          build/hv_reset/gnu/build.sh to a copy of
                          support/aschk
    patches/mdtools/gnu/  applied by build/mdtools.mk to a copy of the
                          mdgen/mdlint sources

To add one: write the diff, drop it in the right subdirectory, and name it where that component applies its patches; the order
there is the apply order:
    patches/hv/           a `$(PATCH) ... -i` line in build/hv_reset.mk, and the same patch in build/hv_reset/gnu/build.sh
    patches/hv/gnu/       a `patch` line in build/hv_reset/gnu/build.sh
    patches/obp/forth/    a `$(PATCH) ... -i` line in build/obp.mk (sun path) and the OBP_PATCHES list in build/obp/gnu/obp-gnu.mk (gnu path)
    patches/obp/sun/      a `$(PATCH) ... -i` line in build/obp.mk
    patches/obp/gnu/      the engine's own build, build/obp/gnu/engine/Makefile
    patches/mdtools/gnu/  the call of build/mdtools/gnu/build.sh in build/mdtools.mk


The patches
-----------
Path relative to patches/, then what it does. Rationale is in each file's
header.

    hv/hv-pcie-ra-segments.patch                        both paths
        Enable the hypervisor's generic RA->PA I/O-segment tier for the
        guest's QEMU-emulated PCIe window.

    hv/hv-sun-strip-debug.patch                         sun path
        Drop Sun cc's debug stubs from the objects before the link, so that
        q.bin does not carry the build directory.

    hv/hv-ds12-offsets-dwarf.patch                      sun path, when the cc
        Make offsets.h and offsets.chk from DWARF, for a cc that writes no
        stabs (Oracle Developer Studio 12.6). See build/hv_reset/README.dwarf.

    hv/gnu/aschk-host-build.patch                       gnu path
        Make Sun's aschk (the check of the assembler sources against
        offsets.chk) run on a Linux host: a one-byte stack overflow in reading
        offsets.chk and a double free in the scanner, both invisible on Solaris.

    mdtools/gnu/mdgen-mdlint-host-endian.patch
        Give mdgen/mdlint's network-byte-order macros a little-endian arm
        (Sun's #else is `#error`), and add the hton64() Sun forgot on integer
        properties in output_bin.c.

    mdtools/gnu/mdgen-mdlint-printf-int64.patch
        %llx/%lld -> PRIx64/PRId64 for uint64_t in the --text/--dot writers;
        no output change, silences five -Wformat warnings on LP64.

    obp/gnu/engine-getmem-mprotect-exec.patch
        The Forth engine's getmem() must mprotect() its arena executable: the
        dictionary it loads is SPARC machine code entered as a function
        pointer, and Linux (unlike Solaris) gives malloc'd memory no PROT_EXEC.

    obp/gnu/makeprom-ptr-roundup.patch
        makeprom's ROUNDUP() truncates a pointer to int on LP64; use a
        pointer-width form at its two call sites. sys/dropins.h is untouched.

    obp/gnu/engine-tools-c99-decls.patch
        Twelve declarations GCC 14 rejects by default (implicit function,
        implicit int, return without value) in the engine and host tools.
        One of them, sigset via s_signal(), truncated a pointer on LP64.

    obp/gnu/printf-widths.patch
        Nine printf widths in makeprom.c/makedi.c/fsys.c that assumed ILP32;
        all on verbose/debug paths. No output change, clean -Wformat.

    obp/gnu/engine-warning-cleanups.patch
        The engine's last warnings: `#endif SCCS` labels, (void) on
        warn_unused_result calls, getwd -> getcwd with the bound. Zero left.

    obp/sun/elf2bin-keep-section-gap.patch
        elf2bin: keep the gap between sections whatever address the first one
        has. Without it, Developer Studio 12.6's decomp.o was placed wrong in
        reset.bin and the PROM printed nothing.

    obp/forth/ophir-qemu-e1000.patch
        Add a QEMU-e1000 (82540EM) as branch to Sun's Ophir (82571) FCode; the
        82571 path is unchanged.

    obp/forth/ophir-skip-eeprom-mac-sync.patch
        Take the e1000 MAC from the chip's MAC registers (i.e. -device
        e1000,mac=...), not from an MD node.

    obp/forth/md-iodevice-reg-guard.patch
        On QEMU's flat PCIe bus (pci@0), keep OBP's MD-iodevice->device match
        from hanging on a reg-less child of the root nexus -- a hang that
        happens during OBP init, before its banner.

    obp/forth/ide-srst-no-bsy-check.patch
        Let OBP's IDE probe detect a drive under QEMU, whose ATA software
        reset finishes too fast for the BSY check (currently for cmd646).
